The Desk
A 1-bit film for the Atlanta Design Festival's Industry Resources, made entirely in code.
No stock footage, no generated video, no photographs, no third-party imagery.

TYPEFACES
  Anton — Vernon Adams and contributors — SIL Open Font License 1.1
    Stamps and stencils: the hook, the figures, the headings.
  Courier Prime — Quote-Unquote Apps — SIL Open Font License 1.1
    Labels, the screen and the typed lines.
  Archivo — Omnibus-Type — SIL Open Font License 1.1
    The printed mastheads.
  Licence texts ship beside the fonts in fonts/. Every word in the film is drawn on an object's
  own canvas and dithered with it: there are no overlay captions.

ENGINE
  The 1-bit pipeline (pipe.js: shading, surface-anchored G-buffer, the two-ink pass, and the
  presenter that mixes, inverts and wipes two 1-bit images) and the kit (kit.js: printed-paper
  and halftone materials, text canvases, screen-space boxes for the reading check) come from the
  Lemo-Opuscar 1-bit Dither demo and are the engine this style ships for the purpose.
  github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar, code MIT. The lossless renderer (tools/render.mjs) is the
  same demo's, patched only so it finds the library through LIB rather than a fixed path.

  The world, the two inks, the shot list, the cameras, the printed surfaces, the score and the
  timing are this film's own. None of the demo's story, sets, props or timings are in it, and no
  game, film or product named in the style's reference list is copied or named here.

  three.js r170 (MIT) renders the scene.

SOUND
  Score and foley synthesised in this project (mix.py) with numpy and scipy: bass clarinet,
  glockenspiel, pizzicato low strings and a detuned upright piano, over a relay, a print head,
  a drum motor, stamps on cork, card slaps, paper and a drawer. No sample libraries, no
  recordings, no third-party audio. No narration: the brief asked for density and pace, and in
  this medium a stamp lands in two frames where a spoken line costs four seconds.

PICTURE
  Rendered at 960×540 internally and scaled with nearest neighbour, as the style requires, then
  captured as lossless PNG into an FFV1 master and encoded to H.264 exactly once. Three lossy
  generations would smear the dot edges into grey.

CONTENT
  Every figure is from the client's Industry Resources 2027 kit: 8,911 industry subscribers,
  39% average open against a trade average near 21%, 19% average click, 0.2% unsubscribe, three
  banner sizes, three posts, four slots a year with one sponsor in each, and the 2027 founding
  rate of $2,500 which the kit states rises to $5,000 for 2028. The film quotes rates and the
  published inventory and promises no reach.

